      <Comment>Lysolecithins, or acyl-&lt;i&gt;sn&lt;/i&gt;-glycero-3-phosphocholines, are derivatives of phosphatidylcholine, resulting from hydrolytic removal of one of the two acyl groups. The instances of this class include different variations based on the specific acyl group which has been removed. The structure below is an example of such an instance.</Comment>
